From 7dc26ac86630d2cbfe226ec469e1792e4d6c8d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:23:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] bcm2835-sdiod: start the Wi-Fi firmware, read its
 version and MAC address

After the chip ID: list the backplane cores from the enumeration ROM,
read the ARM CR4's RAM size, hold the ARM, write firmware and NVRAM (read
back to check), start the ARM, wait for the HT clock and function 2, and
send two firmware commands over the SDPCM/BCDC control channel: "ver"
and "cur_etheraddr". Firmware and NVRAM come from
/usr/lib/firmware/brcm (package wifi-firmware); without them the probe
stops after the chip ID as before.

CMD53 now also writes and uses block mode. The layout of the enumeration
ROM, NVRAM block and frames follows OpenBSD's bwfm(4) and Linux'
brcmfmac (both ISC); unit tests for those three parts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
